Changes relative to the ScalableLux base (full rationale and measurements in
docs/PORT-LUCIS-IDEAS.md and docs/LS2-PLAN.md of the source tree)
  1. Identity: modId `lucistarlink`, display name `LuciStarlink`, entrypoint/command/mixin-config renamed.
     Internal ScalableLux identifiers (the `scalablelux$` mixin member prefix, the
     `ca.spottedleaf.starlight` packages) are deliberately kept so the origin of every file stays visible.
  2. Telemetry: periodic `SLTELEM` line (queue depth, dirty positions, pooled propagators),
     `-Dscalablelux.telemetrySeconds` (default 30, 0 disables).
  3. Commands: `/lucistarlink stats | light <pos> | relight <radius>` (permission level 2).
  4. Client update path: `SWMRNibbleArray.updateVisible()` no longer publishes a nibble whose bytes are
     unchanged (identity-preserving: only when the on-wire content is byte-identical).
  5. Instrumentation: `ca.spottedleaf.starlight.common.debug.LuxProfiler`, off unless `-Dscalablelux.profile=true`.
  6. An optional, default-off scheduling batch (`-Dscalablelux.batchLimit`) kept for A/B experiments only;
     measured neutral, not enabled.
  7. The light computation itself is unchanged. The main repository's differential probe measures this build as
     bit-identical to vanilla on a 599,040-cell box once the engine has settled.
